Body:
I noticed when trying this out with gemini-cli that gemini does not respect the permission settings in my `opencode.jsonc`.

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "gemini-acp-provider": {
      "name": "Gemini Cli",
      "models": {
        "auto": {
          "id": "gemini-3-pro-preview",
          "name": "Gemini 3 Pro"
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "command": "gemini",
        "args": [
          "--experimental-acp"
        ]
      }
    }
  },
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "agent": {
    "build": {
      "permission": {
        "edit": "ask"
      }
    }
  },
  "autoupdate": false
}
```

Is this a limitation of the LLM being provided via ACP @aweis89 ?
Regular models do respect this setting.

@mzealey you can do this in ur opencode config:
```
 "agent": {
    "compaction": {
      "model": "...",
    },
  },
```
